18 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 19 0 R/Alt(Map of U.S. states comparing the share of AI bills that became law in 2025 and 2026 with the share of all bills that became law. Nationally the two are about the same, 17 and 16 percent. Four Southern states pass AI bills much less often than their other bills: Tennessee 20 vs. 44 percent, Virginia 21 vs. 39, Georgia 10 vs. 25, and Louisiana 33 vs. 55. Four states pass AI bills more often: California 52 vs. 43, Connecticut 23 vs. 8, Minnesota 7 vs. 1, and Missouri 9 vs. 3. Each tested state is labeled with the gap in percentage points, from Tennessee at minus 24 to Connecticut at plus 15. Most other states show no clear difference, and 20 states had fewer than 30 AI bills.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[5]/Pg 359 0 R>>
endobj
